  bootwright / policy set
      Validate and atomically replace the delegated SSH session policy of the selected context.
      Requires exactly one --file. --check runs the same validation and writes nothing. Either
      way the result lists every grant of the document with all its subjects and its expanded
      Machines.

  Usage
    bootwright policy set [flags]

  Command flags
      --check     Validate and expand the policy without writing it
      -f, --file  Read one standalone SessionAccessPolicy YAML document (required)

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright policy set --file sessions.yaml
